  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151358/assets/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nLet's now look at the terms one by one.\n\n- The given figure is a quadrilateral with angles that are not all right. So it is **not** a square.\n\n- Since the four sides of the quadrilateral are congruent, it is a rhombus.\n\n- The quadrilateral is a rhombus. A rhombus is a parallelogram where all four sides are equal. So it is a parallelogram.\n\nConsequently, the given shape is described by terms II (rhombus), and III (parallelogram).",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-74510\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-74510-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-74510-e-0\"></div>\n\n<p>Let's now look at the terms one by one.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The given figure is a quadrilateral with angles that are not all right. So it is <strong>not</strong> a square.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Since the four sides of the quadrilateral are congruent, it is a rhombus.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The quadrilateral is a rhombus. A rhombus is a parallelogram where all four sides are equal. So it is a parallelogram.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Consequently, the given shape is described by terms II (rhombus), and III (parallelogram).</p>\n</div>",
